{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#112","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#112","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#112\",\"parent_revision\":\"2bc9cae6e5753477107ea300f7c0441dc8f8655d1d0d1557c010f4f65165db9e\",\"root_revision\":\"2bc9cae6e5753477107ea300f7c0441dc8f8655d1d0d1557c010f4f65165db9e\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## The Recurring Defect\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nA provenance audit of the 25 rules that carried an `origin` with no `reference` found the same failure repeatedly: **a rule hardcodes an enumerated set, upstream moves on, and skilllint emits false positives with no mechanism to notice.**\\n\\nThis is not four bugs. It is one bug with four instances, and patching the four guarantees a fifth.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Confirmed Live Instances\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAll verified against documentation fetched this week via `skilllint docs fetch` into `.claude/vendor/sources/`.\\n\\n### HK002 \u2014 `VALID_EVENT_TYPES` is 9 events behind\\n\\n`packages/skilllint/rules/hk_series.py` holds **22** event names. `code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks.md` documents **31**. Missing: `Setup`, `UserPromptExpansion`, `PermissionDenied`, `PostToolBatch`, `MessageDisplay`, `TaskCreated`, `CwdChanged`, `DirectoryAdded`, `FileChanged`.\\n\\nA plugin registering any of those gets an **error** today. No removals \u2014 the set is a strict subset, so this is pure staleness, not drift in both directions.\\n\\nWorth recording: `docs/design-rule-provenance-registry.md` claims 12 of the current 22 names have \\\"no traceable vendor source\\\". **That claim is wrong** \u2014 all 12 appear verbatim in both the 2026-03-23 and 2026-08-28 captures. The audit that produced it was run against a cache nobody had refreshed. The failure mode is the reverse of what was recorded: not invented constraints, but a set that stopped keeping up.\\n\\n### HK003 \u2014 `VALID_HOOK_TYPES` missing `mcp_tool`\\n\\nHolds `{command, http, prompt, agent}`; docs document **five**. Verbatim from the Common fields table:\\n\\n> `type` | yes | `\\\"command\\\"`, `\\\"http\\\"`, `\\\"mcp_tool\\\"`, `\\\"prompt\\\"`, or `\\\"agent\\\"`\\n\\n`mcp_tool` also has its own required fields (`server`, `tool`) absent from HK003's required-field table. A valid `mcp_tool` handler is an error today.\\n\\n### PL006 \u2014 closed marketplace root-key allowlist\\n\\n`{metadata, name, owner, plugins}`. Upstream documents `$schema`, `description`, `version`, `allowCrossMarketplaceDependenciesOn`, `renames` as valid root fields, plus `forceRemoveDeletedPlugins` in the schemastore schema \u2014 which notably does **not** set `additionalProperties: false`. Five valid keys are errors. (The destructive auto-fix on the same rule is tracked separately; this issue is only the allowlist.)\\n\\n### NR001 \u2014 `BUILTIN_AGENTS` is a 35-name hand-maintained mirror\\n\\nUpstream documents **six** built-in subagents. The frozenset matches four, omits `claude` and `claude-code-guide`, includes `Bash` (a *tool*), and adds 29 names that are this machine's own plugin agents. Its guard is additionally **provably unreachable** \u2014 every extraction regex requires a `:` and captures a 1+-char plugin group, so the `not plugin` condition never holds.\\n</div>\\n\\n## The Designed Answer Exists And Was Never Built\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n`docs/design-rule-provenance-registry.md` specifies a Rule \u2192 Claim \u2192 Authority \u2192 Extraction \u2192 Comparison \u2192 Update pipeline keyed on `packages/skilllint/schemas/provenance-registry.json`.\\n\\n**That file does not exist.** The design is sound and the diagnosis in its problem statement is exactly this issue. What is missing is the first concrete slice.\\n</div>\\n\\n## What Needs Deciding\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n1. **Where sourced constants live.** Python literals with mandatory provenance comments, JSON under `schemas/`, or generated from fetched docs \u2014 there is precedent for the third in `scripts/fetch_spec_schema.py` \u2192 `_spec_constants.py`.\\n2. **How drift becomes a failing check** rather than a silent false positive. `.claude/vendor/` is a gitignored cache and `scripts/fetch_platform_docs.py` already emits `.drift-pending.json`, so what runs in CI versus on demand needs to be concrete.\\n3. **The type contract.** `RuleAuthority.reference` is `str | None`, and that optionality is what let 25 rules ship with no citation. Making it required is tempting \u2014 but **OPINION rules must stay expressible**. SL001 (symlink target hygiene) and LK001 (link validity) are sound rules with genuinely no vendor source. If tightening the contract forces someone to invent a citation for those, the cure is the disease.\\n4. **Migration order** for the four instances, shipping value early.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Related\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- Depends on nothing; blocks nothing. The four instances can be patched independently, but doing so without item 2 means this recurs.\\n- #109 (agent tools-field validation) and #40 (rule-content drift) touch adjacent ground but are not this.\\n- AS007 was deleted for a related-but-distinct defect: a citation that pointed at an anchor which never existed, rather than a set that went stale.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"3e0f7d12468fd1c616eb44f2643d70bca2e0bae38c0791e373f8d86252647445\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDORXxKvc8AAAABXP-Gjg\"}"}